    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d124">

                <pb facs="0111" n="91" sameAs="frus:frus1864p3/pg91"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Dayton</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 564.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1864-05-31"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >May</hi> 31, 1864.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: I have received your despatch of the 16th
                    of May, No. 466, and I am gratified to learn that the explanations you have made
                    concerning the temporary inconveniencies resulting from the postponement of the
                    intended visit of French officers and from the present suspension of the
                    privilege conceded for the removal of French tobacco have been made in so
                    satisfactory a manner.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">William L. Dayton</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
